{#
Month: a six-week grid that fills its container.

The grid itself — the weekday strip, the six equal rows, the hairline gutters
and the today/weekend/spill-in treatment of a cell — lives in
calendar/_month_shell.html.twig, which the public shared-calendar page embeds
too. What is left here is the only part that is about THIS calendar: the "new
event on this day" affordance, the chips that open an editor, and the link to
the day when a cell has more than fits. The shell's own header says why it is a
shell rather than two files that look alike.

Always six weeks, never five-or-six. The range enum asks for 42 days from the
Monday on or before the first, so the grid does not change height between
months — a calendar that reflows as you page through it is disorienting, and it
means the surrounding layout never has to reserve for the taller case.

`grid-rows-6` with `h-full` is what makes the six weeks share the height evenly
instead of each row shrinking to its busiest cell, which left a ragged block of
empty space under the grid. Both are the shell's defaults, so this passes
neither.
#}

{# The view's clock, not the reader's: the day keys are grouped in it, so asking
   a different one which day is today highlights the wrong cell for however many
   hours the two are apart. #}
{% set today = 'now'|date('Y-m-d', range.zone) %}

{# The day the list under a narrow month starts on: today when it is in the
   six weeks on screen, otherwise the first of the month being shown. #}
{% set firstOfMonth = (days|keys)|filter(k => k|date('j') == '1' and k|date('n') == anchor|date('n'))|first %}
{% set selectedDay = today in days|keys ? today : firstOfMonth %}

{# **A month too narrow for words is the grid AND the day under it (#253).**
   Below 39rem a day is under 5.5rem wide (39 rather than 38.5, for the six
   1px gutters, so no width has bars and no list) and its entries are bars (see
   _event_chip), which give the shape of the month and nothing else. So there
   the grid stops filling the pane and keeps six short rows, and the space it
   gives up lists one day in full: today at first, then whichever day was
   tapped. It is the arrangement every phone calendar has, and for the reason
   they have it: a month on a phone is an overview, and what a day holds is read
   in a list, not in a 49px box.

   Every day's list is rendered and all but one hidden, so choosing a day is a
   matter of showing it, with no request and nothing to wait for; a month is at
   most 42 short lists. See calendar/month_tap_controller.js for the tap, which
   on a wider month opens the day's card instead.

   A container query on this wrapper rather than a viewport breakpoint, for the
   reason the chip gives: the same phone-sized width is a month in the pane and a
   month on a page. #}
<div class="@container/month h-full min-h-0 flex flex-col"
     data-controller="calendar--month-tap calendar--now"
     data-calendar--month-tap-selected-value="{{ selectedDay }}"
     {# Today's circle moves at midnight: calendar--now redraws the view when the
        date changes. #}
     data-calendar--now-zone-value="{{ range.zone }}"
     data-calendar--now-today-value="{{ today }}"
     data-action="click->calendar--month-tap#tap:capture keydown.esc@window->calendar--month-tap#close click@window->calendar--month-tap#outside">
{# The ring on the chosen day is drawn only where there is a list for it to
   name. The pointer is on every day: a click on one selects it below 39rem and
   opens its card on a touch screen above. #}
{% embed 'calendar/_month_shell.html.twig' with {
    dayKeys: days|keys,
    days: days,
    anchorMonth: anchor|date('n'),
    today: today,
    shellCellExpands: true,
    shellOuterClass: 'min-h-0 flex flex-col flex-1 @max-[39rem]/month:flex-none @max-[39rem]/month:h-[20rem]',
    shellCellClass: 'cursor-pointer @max-[39rem]/month:data-[selected]:after:pointer-events-none @max-[39rem]/month:data-[selected]:after:absolute @max-[39rem]/month:data-[selected]:after:inset-0 @max-[39rem]/month:data-[selected]:after:z-10 @max-[39rem]/month:data-[selected]:after:ring-2 @max-[39rem]/month:data-[selected]:after:ring-inset @max-[39rem]/month:data-[selected]:after:ring-accent',
} %}
    {% block cell_actions %}
        <button type="button"
           data-controller="ui--modal"
           data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
           data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_calendar_event_new', { start: dayKey }) }}"
           data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.event.new'|trans }}"
           aria-label="{{ 'calendar.event.new_on'|trans({ '%date%': dayKey|intl_date('EEEdMMM') }) }}"
           class="w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-md text-[10px] text-ink-faint
                  opacity-0 day-open:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 @max-[5.5rem]:hidden
                  hover:bg-hover transition-opacity
                  focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent"
        ><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
    {% endblock %}

    {% block cell_date %}
        {# The way into a day. This grid reached one only through "N more",
           which appeared on busy days and nowhere else, and that link is gone
           along with the count it could not get right. The number itself is
           what every calendar anybody has used puts the link on. #}
        <a href="{{ path('app_calendar_view', { view: 'day', date: dayKey }) }}{{ isPane|default(false) ? '?pane=1' : '' }}"
           {% if frame|default(null) %}data-turbo-frame="{{ frame }}"{% endif %}
           aria-label="{{ 'calendar.open_day'|trans({ '%date%': dayKey|intl_date('EEEdMMM') }) }}"
           class="rounded-md hover:bg-hover transition-colors
                  focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">
            {% if isToday %}
                <span class="w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-full
                             bg-accent text-accent-ink text-xs font-semibold tabular-nums">
                    {{ dayKey|date('j', false) }}
                </span>
            {% else %}
                <span class="block px-1 text-xs tabular-nums
                             {{ isOtherMonth ? 'text-ink-faint' : 'text-ink-muted' }}">
                    {{ dayKey|date('j', false) }}
                </span>
            {% endif %}
        </a>
    {% endblock %}

    {% block cell_body %}
        {# **Every entry is drawn and the BOX decides how many are seen.**
           This was a slice to two with a "+1 more" under it, and the report was
           the obvious one: there was room for a third. There always might be. A
           month cell's height is the pane's divided by six, a chip is one row
           or two depending on whether its entry has a time, and no number
           written here can be right for both a tall window and a short one.

           So nothing is counted. The list holds the whole day, the box clips
           it, and a mask fades the last few pixels so a cut chip reads as "this
           goes on" rather than as a rendering fault. Where it goes on to is the
           day's peek, which needs no count either, and the date, which is a
           link now — see the shell's `cell_date`. Gone with the count is "N
           more", and with it the only reason a cell ever spent a row on
           something that was not an event.

           Hovering a day enlarges the whole cell — the shell's card, see
           `shellCellExpands` there, which is where the no-movement rule is set
           out. All this list does about it is stop clipping: the card is what
           decides how far it opens, and it scrolls past the bottom of the grid.

           Titles stay clamped to two lines while it is open — see the chip,
           which says when a title still closes up to one. 18rem is where the
           widening stops, which is about thirty-five characters. #}
        <div class="min-h-0 flex-1 space-y-0.5 overflow-hidden
                    day-open:overflow-visible day-open:shrink-0
                    [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,black_calc(100%-0.625rem),transparent)]
                    day-open:[mask-image:none]">
            {% for cluster in dayEntries %}
                {% include 'calendar/_event_chip.html.twig' with { monthCell: true } %}
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

<section class="hidden @max-[39rem]/month:block flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto border-t border-line"
         aria-live="polite">
    {% for dayKey, dayEntries in days %}
        <div data-calendar--month-tap-target="list" data-list-day="{{ dayKey }}"
             {% if dayKey != selectedDay %}hidden{% endif %}>
            {# The day's own "new event", with the day filled in: the cell's
               hover button cannot be reached on a phone, and this is where the
               reader is looking when they decide the day needs one. #}
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 px-3 pt-2 pb-1">
                <h3 class="text-xs font-medium {{ dayKey == today ? 'text-accent' : 'text-ink' }}">
                    {{ dayKey|intl_date('EEEEdMMMM') }}
                </h3>
                <button type="button"
                   data-controller="ui--modal"
                   data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
                   data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_calendar_event_new', { start: dayKey }) }}"
                   data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.event.new'|trans }}"
                   aria-label="{{ 'calendar.event.new_on'|trans({ '%date%': dayKey|intl_date('EEEdMMM') }) }}"
                   class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg shrink-0
                          bg-accent text-accent-ink hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity
                          focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1"
                ><i class="fa-solid fa-plus text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
            </div>
            {% if dayEntries is empty %}
                <p class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-ink-faint">{{ 'calendar.empty_day'|trans }}</p>
            {% else %}
                {# The agenda's rows: the same three tracks, so a day here reads
                   exactly as it does in that view. #}
                <div class="grid gap-x-2 px-3 pb-3"
                     style="grid-template-columns: fit-content(7rem) max-content minmax(0, 1fr)">
                    {% for cluster in dayEntries %}
                        {% include 'calendar/_event_chip.html.twig' with {
                            showRange: true,
                            timeColumn: true,
                            tooltip: false,
                            dayKey: dayKey,
                        } %}
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
</section>
</div>
